# What the SDIST carries. Declared rather than left to setuptools'
# defaults, which pick up `tests/test_*.py` and NOT support files beside
# them -- a conftest, a shared fixture module, an __init__.
#
# This distribution has no such files today, so its sdist was correct
# WITHOUT this file. That is accident, not agreement: the first conftest
# anyone adds here would vanish from the sdist silently, and the released
# suite would stop collecting while everything checked in this repository
# stayed green. Its sibling `canonical-state` has a conftest, hit exactly
# that, and is where the rule was found.
include LICENSE
include NOTICE
include README.md
include pyproject.toml
recursive-include tests *.py
global-exclude __pycache__
global-exclude *.py[cod]
